Introduction to Computer (BCA Semester 1 Notes)
Definition
A computer is an electronic device that accepts data as input, processes it according to instructions, stores it, and produces meaningful information as output.

Basic Functions of a Computer
A computer performs four basic functions.

1. Input
The computer accepts data from the user.
Examples:
Keyboard
Mouse
Scanner
Microphone

2. Processing
The CPU processes the input data according to instructions.
Example:
25 + 15 = 40

3. Storage
The computer stores data and information for future use.
Examples
Hard Disk (HDD)
SSD
Pen Drive
RAM

4. Output
The computer displays the processed information.
Examples
Monitor
Printer
Speaker

Components of a Computer
A computer has two main components.

1. Hardware
Hardware means the physical parts of a computer that we can see and touch.
Examples
Monitor
Keyboard
Mouse
CPU Cabinet
Printer

2. Software
Software is a set of programs or instructions that tells the computer what to do.
Examples
Windows
Linux
MS Word
Google Chrome

Characteristics of a Computer

1. Speed
A computer works very fast and performs millions of calculations in seconds.

2. Accuracy
It gives accurate results if the input is correct.

3. Storage
It can store a large amount of data.

4. Diligence
It does not become tired or bored.

5. Versatility
It can perform different types of tasks.

6. Automation
Once instructions are given, it works automatically.

7. Reliability
It provides consistent and dependable results.

Applications of Computer
Computers are used in many fields.
Education
Banking
Hospitals
Business
Government
Entertainment
Communication
Science & Research
Transportation
E-commerce

Advantages of Computer:-
High speed
High accuracy
Large storage capacity
Saves time
Multitasking
Automation
Easy communication

Limitations of Computer:-
Cannot think like humans.
Has no emotions.
Depends on user instructions.
Wrong input gives wrong output (GIGO – Garbage In, Garbage Out).
Requires electricity to operate.

1. Types of Computer Based on Working Principle
A) Analog Computer
Definition
An Analog Computer processes continuous data (data that changes continuously).

Features
Works with continuous values.
Gives approximate results.
Used in scientific and engineering fields.

Examples
Speedometer
Thermometer
ECG machine

B) Digital Computer
Definition
A Digital Computer processes discrete (binary) data such as 0 and 1.

Features
Gives accurate results.
Fast and reliable.
Most commonly used computer.

Examples
Desktop
Laptop
Smartphone
Calculator

C) Hybrid Computer
Definition
A Hybrid Computer combines the features of both Analog and Digital computers.

Features
High speed
High accuracy
Used where both continuous and digital data are required.

Examples
ICU monitoring systems
Weather forecasting systems
Aircraft control systems

2. Types of Computer Based on Purpose
A) General Purpose Computer
Definition
A General Purpose Computer is designed to perform many different tasks.

Examples
Desktop
Laptop
Smartphone

B) Special Purpose Computer
Definition
A Special Purpose Computer is designed to perform only one specific task.

Examples
ATM
Traffic light control system
Washing machine controller

3. Types of Computer Based on Size and Performance
A) Microcomputer
Definition
A Microcomputer is a small computer designed for one user.

Features
Single user
Low cost
Commonly used at home, school, and office

Examples
Desktop
Laptop
Tablet
Smartphone

B) Minicomputer
Definition
A Minicomputer is more powerful than a microcomputer and supports multiple users.

Features
Multi-user
Medium-sized organizations
Moderate processing power
Examples
Departmental servers
Small business servers

C) Mainframe Computer
Definition
A Mainframe Computer is a very powerful computer used to process large amounts of data for hundreds or thousands of users simultaneously.

Features
Very high speed
Large storage
Supports many users
Highly reliable

Examples
Banks
Airlines
Government departments
Insurance companies

D) Supercomputer
Definition
A Supercomputer is the fastest and most powerful type of computer.

Features
Extremely high processing speed
Handles complex calculations
Used for scientific research

Examples
Weather forecasting
Space research
Nuclear research
Artificial Intelligence
Climate modeling

